## 1. Entry Preconditions & Unreachable-Tool Rule (`A1`, `A7`)

Verify every item below before executing the first test case:
- [ ] **Code Review Sign-Off (`A1`)**: Code review verdict is `APPROVED` on target revision `{{revision_notation}}` (`{{review_report_location}}`).
- [ ] **Security Review Hand-Off (`A1`, `A6`, `SR14`)**: When security triggers matched, `security-review` verdict and any `Role × Environment × Action × Object` matrix rows or runtime-dependent `PLAUSIBLE` checks are loaded from `{{security_report_location}}`.
- [ ] **Approved Test Plan (`A1`)**: Test cases, expected results, and regression guards are approved in `{{plan_location}}` ({{quality_planning_link}}).
- [ ] **Prepared Environment (`A1`)**: Target environment (`{{mutable_environments}}`) is running revision `{{revision_notation}}` with deterministic seed data per {{quality_environment_link}}.
- [ ] **Verification Tools Reachable (`A7`)**: Primary UI tool (`{{ui_tool}}`, fallback `{{ui_fallback}}`) and API tool (`{{api_tool}}`, fallback `{{api_fallback}}`) respond to health checks. If both primary and fallback tools for a surface fail, mark all cases requiring that surface **`BLOCKED`** citing the exact tool error — never infer or fabricate observations.

